      "report_date": "2026-11-24",
      "title": "clampony npm Dropper Stages a Windows Credential Stealer",
      "summary": "Two npm packages, clampony and safeclamp3, copy a clamp utility and add a preinstall hook that, in clampony, downloads a Windows credential stealer from Pastebin on every install. The stealer collects cloud, SSH, package registry, FTP, shell history and Telegram session data and uploads it to a Telegram bot. It also downloads enterotoxin.exe, a remote-access trojan with keylogging and clipboard capture. The npm dropper does not yet write or run the payload, though safeclamp3 has tested a hidden background launch. Defenders should remove these packages, rotate credentials on any Windows machine that installed a newer version, and check for the RAT and rewritten taskbar shortcuts.",
