      "report_date": "2026-11-24",
      "title": "Webworm APT: Threat Intelligence Analysis Report",
      "summary": "China-aligned Webworm APT group continued operating in 2025, using two new backdoors, EchoCreep and GraphWorm, which use Discord and the Microsoft Graph API (OneDrive) respectively for command-and-control. The group also deploys custom proxy tools, including WormFrp, ChainWorm, SmuxProxy, and WormSocket, to build covert infrastructure. Its targeting has shifted from Asia toward European government institutions, with 2025 victims in Belgium, Italy, Serbia, Poland, and Spain, plus a South African university. Reconnaissance used nuclei and dirsearch, and CVE-2017-7692 (SquirrelMail RCE) was observed as a likely initial access vector. Defenders should prioritize behavior-based detection and cloud traffic analysis, since blocking by IP or domain is less effective against abuse of legitimate cloud services.",
