      "title": "Volant Manticore: Flying Under the Radar",
      "summary": "Check Point Research describes Volant Manticore, a previously undocumented Iran-nexus threat group it assesses has links to Iran's Ministry of Intelligence and Security (MOIS). The group uses the KuboShell backdoor, which relies on IPFS for command-and-control, to deploy the Homa Framework, a reimplementation of MuddyWater's MuddyC2Go client. It targets Cyprus, including telecommunications companies, airlines, and critical infrastructure, and in September 2026 shifted to Saudi healthcare organizations. Researchers assess that the group likely consists of former MuddyWater operators who now run as a separate cluster. Defenders should avoid treating Volant Manticore as part of MuddyWater, as this could create blind spots for organizations in Saudi Arabia and Cyprus.",
