      "report_date": "2026-11-24",
      "title": "Inside a Staged Post-Exploitation Toolkit Targeting Pakistan's Cricket Board: Exchange Webshells, DCSync, and Active Directory Persistence",
      "summary": "An operator exposed a 37-file post-exploitation toolkit on a Latvia-hosted VPS (AS56971) that was used against the Pakistan Cricket Board network. The toolkit uses a compromised Exchange OWA webshell at mail.pcb.com[.]pk as a command relay, masking C2 traffic as legitimate Exchange HTTPS communications. Operators staged DCSync scripts using DSInternals to extract NT hashes from domain controllers without touching LSASS, plus Chisel tunnels for SOCKS proxying and RDP access. Persistence includes a .NET implant with scheduled tasks, a Run key masquerading as Kaspersky tooling, and a malicious Group Policy startup script targeting named machines. Defenders should audit Exchange OWA paths for unexpected ASPX files, block the staging IP, and monitor for unauthorized directory replication and new Run key entries.",
