      "title": "Signed by Microsoft and Mozilla: a Brazilian kit that hands your logged-in browser to an operator",
      "summary": "A Brazilian-targeting browser-hijacking kit, delivered via a per-user MSI named HardwareInfo.msi, side-loads a fake wtsapi32.dll into a renamed copy of the genuine Windows BdeUISrv.exe. The DLL signatures come from a Technoservice B.V. certificate issued through Microsoft Trusted Signing, and the Firefox add-on carries a Mozilla signature. The kit force-installs a malicious extension into Chrome, Edge and Firefox and steals saved passwords and cookies from several browsers. It also prepares a hidden, headless Chrome that an operator can drive remotely while logged in as the victim. Defenders should hunt for the BdeUISrv-based side-loading path, the named scheduled tasks and Startup batch file, and the dead-drop domains.",
